  "description": "Continuous-flow Brayton cycle engines compressing air, burning fuel at constant pressure, and expanding hot gas through axial turbine stages. Achieves 20-40% simple-cycle efficiency and 55-60%+ combined-cycle efficiency (with steam Rankine bottoming cycle), the highest of any commercial power generation technology. Enables jet aviation, peaking power, and high-efficiency baseload generation. Requires nickel superalloys, investment casting, single-crystal blade technology, and ceramic thermal barrier coatings.",
